# Mosquitto ACL template for a Domia mesh. Copy to acl.txt (make mosquitto-acl does this) and
# enable with `acl_file /mosquitto/config/acl.txt` in mosquitto.conf. Topic root = MQTT_TOPIC_ROOT
# (default "domia"). ACL entries after a `user` line apply to that username. With
# allow_anonymous=false, topic lines before the first `user` line (anonymous ACLs) reach no one,
# so every user block must grant the mesh read itself.
#
# Topic layout (all under <root>/…/LOCAL/…):
#   <root>/<domiaKey>/LOCAL/heartbeat        signed identity heartbeat (one per hosted identity)
#   <root>/<domiaKey>/LOCAL/config_changed   live config refresh signal for that identity
#   <root>/<nodeId>/LOCAL/offline            last-will, published by the broker on disconnect
#   <root>/<nodeId>/LOCAL/speaking           speaking / silence broadcast for cross-room courtesy
#
# Every node must READ the whole tree (peer discovery) and WRITE only the topics it owns:
# its hosted identity keys and its own nodeId (GET /identities and /health show them).

# --- one block per node: user = the MQTT username from mqtt_config, the mesh read line plus one
#     write line per hosted identity key and one for the node id
#     (make mosquitto-user USER=<name> PASS=<pass> creates it) ---
user node-a
topic read domia/+/LOCAL/#
topic write domia/DOMIA_A/LOCAL/#
topic write domia/<node-a-nodeId>/LOCAL/#

user node-b
topic read domia/+/LOCAL/#
topic write domia/DOMIA_B/LOCAL/#
topic write domia/<node-b-nodeId>/LOCAL/#

# --- console collector: read-only mirror ---
user collector
topic read domia/#
